Upstream PR: https://github.com/vyperlang/vyper/pull/5282
Status: merged 2026-10-16 (08c2841623c5c0cc2850cc49dbeb79f13d77f940)

Backport the `lower_Assign` hunk only: an assignment whose target indices can
modify memory or storage freezes the right-hand side before lowering the
target, so the store sees the value from before those effects, as legacy
codegen does.

Adapted to this pin: the pin already has `eval_order.py` (with
`expression_can_mutate_memory_or_storage`) and
`snapshot_value_for_delayed_use` in `context.py`, so those hunks are dropped
and only the import and the snapshot in `lower_Assign` are kept. Upstream's
other snapshot conditions there (a source read through an unbounded struct
member's payload, or containing an unbounded sequence) belong to the PR's
unbounded struct member feature and are left out, as is the rest of the PR.

